      "height": 1648,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0",
      "artist": "pfly from Pugetopolis",
      "description": "View from the ferry to Orcas Island.  If I have my geography right, Orcas Island is on the left side, Blakely Island on the right, and Obstruction Island in between.  Behind Obstruction Island is Lummi Island's Lummi Peak, I think.  The strait on the left (north) side of Obstruction Island is Obstruction Pass, while the one on the right (south) is Peavine Pass (mostly hidden from this angle).\n\nThe giant glacier-covered volcano is Mt Baker, and the line of jagged high ridges to the right is, I think, Twin Sisters Mountain.",
